        <property name="plainText">
         <string>Indicator Description:
The KDJ indicator integrates the concepts of momentum, the Relative Strength Index (RSI), and moving averages. It was initially applied to futures trading with notable effectiveness and has since become one of the most widely used indicators in stock markets.
Trading Rules:
1.A downside crossover of the D line by the K line generates a sell signal; an upside crossover generates a buy signal.
2.Two consecutive downside crossovers at high levels confirm a downtrend; two consecutive upside crossovers at low levels confirm an uptrend.
3.D &lt; 20% is oversold; D &gt; 80% is overbought; J &gt; 100% is overbought; J &lt; 10% is oversold.
4.When KD values hover around 50% or cross near that level, the signals are meaningless.
5.This indicator is not applicable to highly speculative individual stocks.
6.Divergence between KD values and price can be observed to confirm market highs and lows.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
